>59384</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Drop a Pair of Five-Set Matches to Round Out the West Virginia Invitational</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/9/11/volleyball-mountaineers-drop-a-pair-of-five-set-matches-to-round-out-the-west-virginia-invitational</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/9/11/volleyball-mountaineers-drop-a-pair-of-five-set-matches-to-round-out-the-west-virginia-invitational</guid><category>Volleyball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="WVU plays Toledo in the West Virginia Invitational on Friday, Sept. 11" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/9/11/4-DSC00501.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The West Virginia University volleyball team (4-3, 0-0 Big 12) battled through a pair of five-set matches Friday at Hope Coliseum, taking a 2-1 lead against Lehigh (7-1, 0-0 Patriot) before falling, 3-2, in the afternoon and dropping another 3-2 decision to Toledo (7-1, 0-0 MAC) in the evening.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/9/11/4-DSC00501.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/9/11/4-DSC00501.jpg"><media:title>WVU plays Toledo in the West Virginia Invitational on Friday, Sept. 11</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/9/11/4-DSC00501.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 23:06:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>17</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59387</s:story_id></item><item><title>Second-Half Onslaught Leads Mountaineers Past Denver</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/9/11/mens-soccer-second-half-onslaught-leads-mountaineers-past-denver</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/9/11/mens-soccer-second-half-onslaught-leads-mountaineers-past-denver</guid><category>Men's Soccer</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Pablo Pozos and Isaac Scheer celebrate after scoring a goal against Denver" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/9/11/9_11_Goal2-2.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – It was a second-half masterclass for the West Virginia University men's soccer team on Friday night as the Mountaineers defeated Denver, 5-0, at Dick Dlesk Soccer Stadium, scoring all five goals after the break. WVU improves to 3-1-1 while the Pioneers fall to 1-5-1.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/9/11/9_11_Goal2-2.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/9/11/9_11_Goal2-2.jpg"><media:title>Pablo Pozos and Isaac Scheer celebrate after scoring a goal against Denver</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/9/11/9_11_Goal2-2.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 23:03:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>6</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59386</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Win RMU Invitational in Season Opener</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/9/11/cross-country-mountaineers-win-rmu-invitational-in-season-opener</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/9/11/cross-country-mountaineers-win-rmu-invitational-in-season-opener</guid><category>Cross Country</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="XC Team" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2025/9/12/MXB_0290.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The West Virginia University cross country team opened the 2026 season with a first-place finish at the RMU 